/////If you want the Back button to return to the previous page (regardless of which route the user came from), 
use Laravel's url()->previous() or the browser history.

Option 1 (Recommended - Laravel)

<a href="{{ url()->previous() }}"
   class="btn btn-secondary"
   style="float:right;">
    <i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i>
    Back
</a>

Option 2 (Browser History)

<a href="javascript:history.back()"
   class="btn btn-secondary"
   style="float:right;">
    <i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i>
    Back
</a>

or

<button type="button"
        class="btn btn-secondary"
        style="float:right;"
        onclick="history.back();">
    <i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i>
    Back
</button>
